// Practice quiz: REST controllers
// Minimum release, November 2026: author-checked, no independent review. Formative, low-stakes retention practice. Titles name the objective id each item practises.

$CATEGORY: spring-boot/spring-boot-basics/rest-controllers

::o1 body output::What does @RestController do to the value a handler returns? {
~Uses it as a view name#Not quite. That is a plain @Controller returning a view.
~Stores it in the session#Not quite. Nothing goes in the session by default.
=Writes it to the response body#Correct. It is serialized, usually as JSON.
~Logs it and returns 204#Not quite. A normal return defaults to 200 with a body.
}

::o1 record output::A handler returns a record with components id and title. What JSON does the client see? {
~A single string from toString#Not quite. It is not written with toString.
~An array of two strings#Not quite. A record maps to a JSON object.
~Nothing, because records cannot be serialized#Not quite. Records serialize normally.
=An object with id and title fields#Correct. Record components are serialized as fields.
}

::o2 Javalin mapping::Which annotation replaces reading ctx.bodyAsClass in a Javalin handler? {
=@RequestBody on a parameter#Correct. It binds the JSON body to the parameter type.
~@PathVariable#Not quite. That binds a path segment.
~@RequestParam#Not quite. That binds a query parameter.
~@ResponseStatus#Not quite. That sets the response status.
}

::o2 same path::A controller has a GET and a POST on the same path. How does Spring pick the handler? {
~Whichever method appears first#Not quite. Source order does not decide this.
=By HTTP method and path together#Correct. Both parts of the mapping must match.
~It fails at startup#Not quite. Different methods on one path is normal.
~By the Java method name#Not quite. The Java name plays no part.
}

::o3 curl defaults::You run curl against a URL with no method flag. Which method is sent? {
~POST#Not quite. POST requires -X POST or -d.
~PUT#Not quite. PUT requires a flag.
~OPTIONS#Not quite. It is not the default.
=GET#Correct. That is curl default for a plain URL.
}

